<%# locals: (playthrough:) %>
<%# THE FACTS CARD AND THE PARAGRAPH BOX, for the turn waiting for the
    player's paragraph in a game they narrate (`Playthrough::Session#waiting`).

    THE CARD IS THE ENGINE'S OWN WORDS, read off the records
    (`Playthrough::Session#facts_card`): what the protagonist did, what the
    arrival found, what the people there did, what the world took, who was hit,
    and the closing words where the turn ended the story. No model wrote any of
    it and none of it is the narrator's instruction-laden fact sentences. It is
    drawn on `.sheet`, the frame the battle panel already uses -- the engine's
    records rendered rather than narrated, which is what this is -- with no new
    colours.

    THE BOX keeps the player's words beside the turn and has them checked
    against its facts; the note the check leaves is shown under the paragraph
    in the log (`turns/_turn`). Nothing a player writes here is read by the
    game. %>
<% session = Playthrough::Session.new(playthrough) %>
<% if (scene = session.waiting) && (card = session.facts_card(scene)) %>
  <div class="sheet facts-card" id="<%= dom_id(scene, :facts) %>">
    <h2>What happened</h2>
    <p class="sheet-lead"><%= card.act %></p>
    <% card.found.each do |fact| %>
      <p class="sheet-note"><%= fact %></p>
    <% end %>
    <% (card.people + card.tolls + card.wounds).each do |fact| %>
      <p class="sheet-note"><%= fact %></p>
    <% end %>
    <% if card.ending %>
      <p class="sheet-lead"><%= card.ending %></p>
    <% end %>
    <p class="sheet-prompt">Your paragraph</p>
    <%= form_with url: playthrough_paragraphs_path(playthrough), class: "paragraph-box" do |form| %>
      <%= form.hidden_field :scene_id, value: scene.id %>
      <%= form.text_area :text, rows: 4, placeholder: "write what happened, as you would tell it",
                                aria: { label: "your paragraph" } %>
      <%= form.submit "Keep my paragraph" %>
    <% end %>
  </div>
<% end %>
